From 90602c005e0234696f295ca6269bb525fc3cd71f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:28:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-58: panel Alignment, on the caption span (0.58.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The generated pages centre every panel caption (.pnlCap { text-align:center }),
but in the DFMs some TPanels are taLeftJustify / taRightJustify -- e.g.
Data.Observer's palCustomer (26 generated panels whose caption is not
centred in BCB6). Alignment now covers generated panels too:
- probe: a <div class="pnl"> with its .pnlCap reads its Alignment from the
  span; setting it writes text-align on the span (target pnlCap), taCenter
  = the declaration removed (the class centres it)
- DFM: a TPanel without Alignment is taCenter (VCL's default)
- the properties panel's Alignment row, the difference list and 改回 DFM
  work as for labels; a panel's font and alignment on the same span are one
  edit (the R45 merge)

Tests: lib (the TPanel default), probe (Panel1 / Panel4: right -> the span,
centre -> removed, the computed alignment follows), real VS Code
(Data.Observer palCustomer: 改回 DFM -> text-align:left on its caption span,
with its bold, ONE undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
